No! I generally like your idea because whenever I get the amulet I'll
wear it till ascension or death. I consider this a bad thing. But the
same problem goes with the BoH: It used to be a major problem (in my
games) to get hold of a BoH. Now when I find one in Sokoban, I'm a 
little bit disappointed (I consider the amulet to let my characyers
live longer) but have solved another problem once and for all.

People in this group will probably argue that this is the point of the
branches - equipping you with valuable items that last throughout the
game. I'd like to see interesting objects somewhat off that mark: what
about "ofMB. Fun + cool, but much weaker than "ofReflection. But the
typical character reaching Sokoban end probably has no amulet, so he
_will_ wear it. When finally an amulet of reflection is found, you
have one more option.

> But you agree that it doesn't have to be a permanent object now?

At least I agree. When I was unspoiled and didn't know about wishing,
I often used a fountain wish for 2 blessed potions of gain ability. 
This is not necessary but so nice. Noone will complain about it. Same
goes for !ofGL except that players will probably not use it immediately
(which prizes should strive for, I think).

